# .apex-ignore
#
# This file specifies files/folders that the APEX instructions agent should COMPLETELY IGNORE
# when analyzing project structure and creating copilot-instructions.md
#
# WHAT "IGNORE" MEANS:
#   - Files/folders matching these patterns are EXCLUDED from analysis
#   - They will NOT be mentioned anywhere in copilot-instructions.md
#   - They will NOT appear in feature lists, module tables, or any documentation
#   - They are treated as if they don't exist in the repository
#
# USE CASES:
#   - Exclude dependencies (node_modules/, vendor/)
#   - Exclude build artifacts (dist/, build/, target/)
#   - Exclude framework/tooling files that aren't your application code
#   - Exclude symlinked directories (.apex/, .github/agents/)
#
# Syntax:
#   - Lines starting with # are comments
#   - Each line specifies a pattern (supports basic glob patterns)
#   - Patterns are matched against file/folder paths relative to project root
#   - Use / for directory separators
#   - Trailing / indicates a directory (all contents ignored)
#   - * matches any sequence of characters (except /)
#   - ** matches any sequence of characters (including /)
#
# Examples:
#   node_modules/           # Ignore node_modules directory
#   dist/                   # Ignore build output directory
#   *.log                   # Ignore all log files
#   temp/**                 # Ignore temp directory and all subdirectories
#   .git/                   # Ignore git metadata
#   **/*.min.js             # Ignore all minified JS files

# Dependencies and package directories
node_modules/
vendor/
venv/
env/
.env/

# Build outputs and generated files
dist/
build/
out/
target/
*.min.js
*.min.css
*.bundle.js

# IDE and editor files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Version control
.git/
.svn/
.hg/

# Logs and temporary files
*.log
logs/
tmp/
temp/
.cache/

# OS-specific files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Test coverage and reports
coverage/
.nyc_output/
test-results/

# Documentation build artifacts
docs/_build/
site/

# GitHub Agents, Skills & Prompts
.github/agents/
.github/skills/
.github/prompts/

# Apex
.apex/scripts/
.apex/templates/
